## JSON → PostgreSQL Migration Path

The `db.js` data is structured so each "table" maps directly to a PostgreSQL `CREATE TABLE`:

```sql
-- Example: users table maps directly from DB_SEED.users
CREATE TABLE users (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  full_name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  role VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('HR_ADMIN','HRMPSB_MEMBER','DEPT_HEAD','APPLICANT','EMPLOYEE')),
  department_code VARCHAR(10),
  is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
  requires_2fa BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

The `NbscDB.exportForPostgres()` method will output JSON that can be directly loaded via `psql \copy` or a migration script.

